KG42.register("rules-3f59ed9f97f841b8818b3769",{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R004","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"The DNO, as local market coordinator, provides the DNEM market clearing price. Scope: DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The DNO, as local market coordinator, provides the DNEM market clearing price. Scope: DNEM in the proposed hierarchical WEM-DNEM electricity market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The DNEM market clearing price provided by the DNO is lambda_0, the Lagrangian multiplier associated with the generation and load balance constraint of the distribution network in the DNEM clearing formulation.","expression":"\\mathrm{MCP}=\\lambda_0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E005","v141-b-g01-E008","v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g01-E015"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E005","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"composed of these markets. Here, each market participant bids in associated electricity market, whil","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Fig. 1 shows the proposed hierarchical market structure that composed of these markets. Here, each market participant bids in associated electricity market, while each LA is an intermediate agent that participates in both markets to address the synergy of the two markets. The LA bids in the WEM and presents the awarded dispatch in the DNEM as demand on its bus in the WEM. The ISO clears the market and provide the awarded dispatch for the LA and LMP at the LAs bus. The LA bids in the DNEM and presents the awarded dispatch in the WEM as demand on its bus in the DNEM. The DNO clears the market and provide the awarded dispatch for the LA and the market clearing price (MCP) of the market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E008","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-B Microgrids Objective","anchor_text":"ds ψ′ ≤ψ′j ≤ψ′j (2) jme- he ρ′j = ψ′j 2αjPje + βj ; Pje = Pj. (3) nd e on B. Microgrids Objective de","equation_id":"(4)-(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Microgrid m maximizes the payoff function (4), subjected to the limitations on the bidding vector as shown in (5). Here, the first term in the payoff function is the revenue of the microgrid and the second term is the generation cost. The generation dispatch of microgrids is provided by curtailing the IL and dispatching the DERs. The microgrid may adopt several policies to serve its demand. One policy is to serve local demand and bid the excess generation in the DNEM while the other is to bid on its total generation capacity in the DNEM and serve the local demand economically from the distribution network. In both cases, the bidding vector for generation in microgrid m is shown in (6)\nR_m = \\max_{P_m,\\psi_m} \\left[ \\lambda_0 \\cdot P_m - \\left(\\alpha_m P_m^2 + \\beta_m P_m + \\gamma_m\\right) \\right] \\tag{4}\n\\underline{\\psi}_m \\le \\psi_m \\le \\bar{\\psi}_m \\tag{5}\n\\rho_m = \\psi_m(2\\alpha_m P_{me} + \\beta_m); \\quad \\sum_e P_{me} = P_m. \\tag{6}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E011","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-C LAs Objective","anchor_text":"of providing electricity to the distribution network. The LAs bidding vector in the DNEM is given in","equation_id":"(10)-(12)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"R'_l = \\max_{\\psi'_l,P_l^{exp}} \\left[ \\left(\\sum_{o\\in B_l^o} LMP'_o - \\lambda_0\\right) P_l^{exp} \\right] \\tag{10}\n\\underline{\\psi}'_l \\le \\psi'_l \\le \\bar{\\psi}'_l \\tag{11}\n\\rho'_l = \\psi'_l * \\lambda_0. \\tag{12}\nConsidering role “2,” the LA l maximizes the payoff function which is shown in (10), subjected to the constraints on the bidding vector (11). The MCP (\\lambda_0) in the DNEM is the marginal cost of providing electricity to the WEM. The bidding vector of LA l in the WEM is shown in (12)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E015","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p04-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-E DNEM Clearing Process","anchor_text":"y As min ρm ∗Pm + ρl ∗Pimpl (19) m l 7) s.t. Pm + Pimpl = PD + Pexpl λ0 (20) m l l 8) P m ≤Pm ≤¯Pm ∀","equation_id":"(19)-(22)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The DNO minimizes the operational cost of distribution network as shown by\n\\min \\sum_m \\rho_m * P_m + \\sum_l \\rho_l * P_l^{imp} \\tag{19}\ns.t. \\sum_m P_m + \\sum_l P_l^{imp} = P^D + \\sum_l P_l^{exp} \\quad \\lambda_0 \\tag{20}\n\\underline{P}_m \\le P_m \\le \\bar{P}_m \\quad \\forall m \\tag{21}\n\\underline{P}_l^{imp} \\le P_l^{imp} \\le \\bar{P}_l^{imp} \\quad \\forall l. \\tag{22}\nThe load balance in the distribution network is shown in (20). The constraints on the awarded generation for microgrids and the imported power by the LA are shown in (21) and (22), respectively. Here, \\lambda_0 is the Lagrangian multiplier for the generation and load balance constraint in the distribution network as it is assumed that the electricity delivery is not limited by the line congestions."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational-decision variable is introduced by this pricing rule. The source defines the DNEM MCP as lambda_0, a Lagrangian multiplier determined endogenously by DNEM clearing, not as an independent decision variable; clearing quantities and constraints belong to the local clearing rule scope.","empty_theta_reason":"The pricing identity contains no fixed numeric coefficient, bound, or parameter value. Demand, generation bounds, line limits and cost coefficients are inputs to clearing or case-study calculations, not parameters of this local-price rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E005","quote":"The DNO clears the market and provide the awarded dispatch for the LA and the market clearing price (MCP) of the market."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"7f2e384808e50bb8baf95c3749c45dc355f62c4aaed0a582ebe064fb47e92761","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The existing C001 remains the procedural statement that the DNO provides the DNEM market clearing price. A source-supported mathematical identity can be added from the same mechanism: the DNEM MCP is identified as lambda_0, the Lagrangian multiplier of the distribution-network generation/load-balance constraint in the DNEM clearing formulation. The rule is therefore formalized at the level of this supported price identity; no independent pricing decision variable is introduced.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The procedural constraint states that the local operator provides the local market clearing price; the frozen edge v141-c-R004-E001 links coordination.local_operator to pricing.local."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The mathematical identity attaches the DNEM MCP lambda_0 to the same local pricing relation: the DNO's local-operator role provides the DNEM clearing price, and the source identifies that price with the Lagrangian multiplier of the DNEM generation/load-balance constraint."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
